            <ArticleTitle>Primary intraosseous squamous cell carcinoma - A rare odontogenic malignancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>320</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/jomfp.JOMFP_25_16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary intraosseous squamous cell carcinoma (PIOSCC) is a rare epithelial odontogenic malignancy affecting the jaws, especially in elderly population. It is a rare lesion, because very few cases of PIOSCC have been reported in the literature with not much of research done on this particular entity. In the present article, we report a case of PIOSCC with detailed discussion of clinical, radiographic and histopathologic features along with review of literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
